description: >
  `persisted_peer_addr` is a private free function that takes a SocketAddr and
  returns it unchanged. It is called at line 227 as
  `peer_addr: persisted_peer_addr(endpoint)`. The function body is a pure
  identity — it neither transforms the address nor reads any persisted state
  despite its name implying it does. It adds indirection with zero semantic
  value and should be removed; the call site should use `endpoint` directly.

pattern: dead/no-op function
